pe="author"><name><surname>Clark</surname><given-names>D.A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Detecting tropical responses to global climatic and atmospheric change: current challenges and a way forward</article-title><source>Biotropica</source><volume>39</volume><year>2007</year><fpage>4</fpage><lpage>19</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.1111/j.1744-7429.2006.00227.x">doi:10.1111/j.1744-7429.2006.00227.x</ext-link></citation></ref><ref id="bib7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Clarke</surname><given-names>D.A</given-names></name><name><surname>Clarke</surname><given-names>D.B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Climate-induced annual variation in canopy tree growth in a Costa Rican tropical rain forest</article-title><source>J. Ecol</source><volume>82</volume><year>1994</year><fpage>865</fpage><lpage>872</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.2307/2261450">doi:10.2307/2261450</ext-link></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Curtis</surname><given-names>P.S</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A meta-analysis of elevated CO<sub>2</sub> effects on woody plant mass, form and physiology</article-title><source>Oecologia</source><volume>113</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>299</fpage><lpage>313</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.1007/s004420050381">doi:10.1007/s004420050381</ext-link></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ehleringer</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Bj&#x000f6;rkman</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Quantum yields for CO<sub>2</sub> uptake in C<sub>3</su