h in tropical forest trees</article-title><source>Ecol. Lett</source><volume>10</volume><year>2007</year><fpage>461</fpage><lpage>469</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.1111/j.1461-0248.2007.01033.x">doi:10.1111/j.1461-0248.2007.01033.x</ext-link><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17498145</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Galmes</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Flexas</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Keys</surname><given-names>A.J</given-names></name><name><surname>Cifre</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Mitchell</surname><given-names>R.A.C</given-names></name><name><surname>Madgwick</surname><given-names>P.J</given-names></name><name><surname>Haslam</surname><given-names>R.P</given-names></name><name><surname>Medrano</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Parry</surname><given-names>M.A.J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Rubisco specificity factor tends to be larger in plant species from drier habitats and in species with persistent leaves</article-title><source>Plant Cell Environ</source><volume>28</volume><year>2005</year><fpage>571</fpage><lpage>579</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.1111/j.1365-3040.2005.01300.x">doi:10.1111/j.1365-3040.2005.01300.x</ext-link></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Graham</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Mulkey</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kitajima</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Phillips</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Wright</surname><given-names>S.J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cloud cover limits net CO<sub>2</sub> uptake and growth of a 